WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:05.660
In this Sprouts video we introduce 7 ways to learn a new language.

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:09.620
“Drown Yourself to Swimming”

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:12.000
Leave the comfort of your home

00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:16.800
and go to the place where they speak nothing but the language that you want to learn.

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:19.860
Then live there for the next 6-12 month.

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:22.520
It might be painful and lonely at times

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:24.840
but you will surely learn how to speak the language

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:28.620
and enjoy some memorable experiences.

00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:31.520
"Immersion"

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:34.860
Perhaps easier and also effective

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:36.080
is immersion

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:40.400
or when you learn a new language through exposure and context.

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:42.300
So, for example,

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:46.080
if you are learning Italian, do so in a Pizzeria.

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:51.340
You can try to read the menu or maybe even go as far as order in Italian

00:00:51.340 --> 00:00:56.360
Antipasti, Pizza Tonno, or Gelato anybody?

00:00:57.220 --> 00:00:59.380
"Mnemonics"

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:03.480
Mnemonics, is a method to learn new vocabulary

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:07.980
by creating an association that makes it easy to remember.

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:09.240
For example,

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:11.880
let’s say you want to remember the French word

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:13.200
“chou”,

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:16.380
which means “cabbage” in English.

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:20.400
“Chou” is pronounced like “shoe” in English,

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:24.200
so you could imagine putting cabbages on your feet instead of shoes.

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:25.060
Then,

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:27.040
when you need to remember “cabbage”,

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:32.520
your brain will think “cabbage -&gt; shoes -&gt; chou”.

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:35.220
"Scriptorium"

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:39.660
Scriptorium is an exercise in writing.

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:44.780
Students write the language while simultaneously speaking it out loud.

00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:48.500
Before you write a sentence you should first read it out loud,

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:52.020
second say each word aloud again as you write it

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:56.920
and third read the sentence aloud again after you have written it.

00:01:56.920 --> 00:02:01.080
The purpose of this exercise is to force yourself to slow down

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:02.920
and pay attention to detail

00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:07.620
and then review unknown words and refresh your grammar.

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:10.280
"Shadowing"

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:13.840
Shadowing is used to learn vocabulary.

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:17.560
You listen to new words through headphones and try to repeat,

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:21.860
to “shadow” them out loud as quickly as you can.

00:02:21.860 --> 00:02:24.060
Inventor Alexander Arguelles,

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:26.120
who speaks 50 languages,

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:32.680
suggests that you do it while walking swiftly to maximise alertness and blood flow!

00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:35.780
"Tech and Apps"

00:02:36.580 --> 00:02:38.480
If you want to learn a new language,

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:40.980
but you don't have anybody who can help,

00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:43.960
check out whats available online.

00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:45.740
DuoLingo for example

00:02:45.740 --> 00:02:49.080
teaches many languages entirely for free.

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:56.160
Its fun and effective as they make you practice reading, writing, listening and speaking.

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:59.840
Quizlet is great tool to study vocabulary.

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:03.420
It allows you to explore audio supported flashcards.

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:07.860
So you can learn new words and get the pronunciation right.

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:11.040
"Get a Study-buddy"

00:03:11.660 --> 00:03:15.320
If you are not into technology and would rather learn with others,

00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:21.120
do what popular YouTuber Timothy Doner aka Polyglot Pal recommends.

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:23.080
Connect with people from around the world

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:26.180
to teach and learn from each other via Skype.

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:28.200
Its one of the things that worked for him

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:33.040
and he already speaks 20 languages and he’s not even 18.

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:35.640
Thanks for watching.

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:38.500
Also check out other Sprouts Learning Techniques,

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:42.640
as they can compliment the methods explained in this video.

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:45.140
Please use the comments below to give us feedback

00:03:45.140 --> 00:03:52.040
or tell us which of the techniques is your favorite, if any!

